course: dictionary
lesson: 788
title: Bedrock: the solid base
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one. «Dig a deep hole in a garden and you see layers» means you are digging into the ground, so bedrock is the solid rock at the bottom, under the soil.
explain: Bedrock has a second meaning too. «Honesty is the bedrock of friendship» means honesty is the basic thing that friendship depends on, like the rock a house stands on. The clue is the phrase the bedrock of. Try the meaning in the sentence: friendship rests on honesty, so it makes sense.
explain: Read the whole sentence before you decide. If it is about digging, layers or the ground, bedrock means the rock. If it is about ideas, values or what something depends on, it means the second meaning. Check your choice by putting it into the sentence.
fact: Bedrock means the solid rock that lies under soil and loose rocks.
fact: «Dig a deep hole in a garden and you see layers: dark crumbly topsoil, paler subsoil under it, then broken rock, and at the bottom solid bedrock.»
fact: Soil has layers called horizons, and broken rock lies above the bedrock.
fact: Bedrock can also mean the basic idea or part that everything else depends on.
fact: Two phrases to know: the bedrock of, as in «the bedrock of friendship», and down to bedrock, which means all the way to the solid rock.
exercise: «Dig a deep hole in a garden and you see layers ... at the bottom solid bedrock.» What is bedrock in this sentence? | A layer of broken rock near the top | *The solid rock under the soil and loose rocks | Paler subsoil | Dark crumbly topsoil
exercise: «Honesty is the bedrock of friendship.» What does bedrock mean here? | The wettest part of a friendship | The rock under a garden | *The basic thing that friendship depends on | A fast game
exercise: Find and copy the word that names the solid rock in this sentence: «Soil has layers called horizons: dark topsoil, paler subsoil below, and broken rock above the bedrock.» | horizons | *bedrock | topsoil | subsoil
test: When you dig down in a garden, which layer do you reach last? | *Bedrock | Topsoil | Broken rock | Subsoil
test: «The bedrock of our club is kindness.» What does bedrock mean? | *The basic idea everything else depends on | A rock you can climb | Something you forget quickly | A type of hard garden soil
exam: In «Soil has layers called horizons: dark topsoil, paler subsoil below, and broken rock above the bedrock», what lies directly above the bedrock? | *Broken rock | Paler subsoil | Horizons | Topsoil
